    tldr: "The first exome study of gallbladder cancer, in 57 Chinese patients, found TP53 mutated in about half and showed that the ErbB family of growth receptors (EGFR, HER2, HER3 and their partners) is the most commonly hit pathway, with a worse outlook when it is.",
